@startuml illustrate-flow
!theme plain
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 200
skinparam wrapWidth 180
title Illustrate: every path from the user pressing "Illustrate"\nto the pictures (or refusals) landing on the chapter node

actor User
participant "ChatNodeComponent\nillustrate()" as UI
participant "IllustrateDialog\n(dialog service + component)" as DLG
participant "Generation config\n(image-create task / settings)" as CFG
participant "ChatService\n(editAssistant)" as SVC
participant "LlmService\ngenerateImage()" as GEN
participant "LlmService\nplanning pass" as PLAN
participant "Provider\n(proxy → /chat/completions + /images)" as NET

== 1. Entry: what the user pressed ==
User -> UI : Illustrate button
note over UI
  Guards first:
  - isGenerating(node) / isLoading → ignore (button disabled)
  - a chapter node can be illustrated directly;
    a direction node needs a current chapter child.
end note
alt on a direction (user node) without a current chapter
  UI -> UI : … no assistant child found
  UI -> User : alert "No chapter to attach to" (imageNoChapter)
  return (nothing happens)
else on a chapter (assistant node) or direction WITH a chapter
  UI -> UI : chapter = target assistant node;\nanchorText = node content (or composer draft);\ncontextParentId = parent branch
end

== 2. Resolve the default rendering model ==
UI -> CFG : modelFor('image-create') + providerFor('image-create')
alt task model configured and enabled
  CFG --> UI : that model + provider
else fallback
  UI -> CFG : first enabled model with canGenerateImages()
  CFG --> UI : model + provider (or null)
end
alt none found
  UI -> User : alert "No image model is enabled" (imageModelMissing)
  return (nothing happens)
end

== 3. Illustrate dialog (seeded + remembered) ==
UI -> DLG : open({ modelId, providerId } = default model)
DLG -> DLG : seed from last-used options;\ndefault model wins over a stale remembered one
alt user clicks Cancel
  DLG --> UI : null
  UI -> UI : return (nothing happens)
else user confirms (count / style / storyboard rules /\nmode: pure picture, model)
  DLG --> UI : {count, style, storyboardPrompt,\npurePictures, modelId, providerId}
end

== 4. Resolve the model chosen in the dialog ==
UI -> CFG : enabled model matching selected modelId + providerId
alt dialog model is valid
  CFG --> UI : chosen model + provider
else empty / stale selection
  UI -> UI : fall back to the default task model
end
alt still no model/provider
  UI -> User : alert "No image model is enabled"
  return
end
UI -> UI : isLoading = true; pendingAction = 'image'

== 5. Build the picture context + anchor ==
UI -> UI : contextMessages = buildContextMessagesUpTo(contextParentId)\nmessages = textOnlyMessages(contextMessages)
UI -> UI : instruction = image-create prompt (or default)\nstyled = instruction + "\\n\\nStyle: …" if a style was chosen
UI -> UI : anchor = styled instruction + "… to illustrate:\\n" + scene text
alt chosen model canInterpretImages AND prior illustrations exist
  UI -> UI : append prior images as image_url parts (max 4)
else
  UI -> UI : plain text anchor only
end

== 6. Resolve the picture-description planner ==
UI -> UI : resolvePlanner() — the model that WRITES\nthe story prefers for pure-text planning
alt node's own writing model resolvable and ≠ image model
  UI -> UI : planner = node model
else image-interpret / language-check task configured
  UI -> UI : planner = that task model
else
  UI -> UI : planner = the image model itself (poor but works)
end

UI -> GEN : generateImage(provider, model, messages, {count,\nstoryboardPrompt, planDescriptions, singleCall,\nplanner, sceneInstruction, purePictures, onProgress})

== 7. generateImage: optional planning pass ==
alt planDescriptions on (storyboard >1, chapter node,\n or pure-picture mode)
  GEN -> PLAN : planStoryboardDescriptions(text model,\n"expand the story into N picture descriptions")
  alt planning call succeeds
    PLAN --> GEN : array of N concrete descriptions
  else planning fails / times out / nothing usable
    PLAN --> GEN : nulls (caller falls back to generic scene instruction)
  end
end

== 8. generateImage: one-shot storyboard (non-pure) ==
alt !purePictures && singleCall && count > 1
  GEN -> GEN : oneShotStoryboardPrompt(base + descriptions,\nstoryboard rules)
  GEN -> NET : ONE completion for all N images (+modalities)
  alt all N images returned
    NET --> GEN : images ≥ count
    GEN --> UI : single scene with all images → done
  else fewer images returned
    NET --> GEN : warn → fall through to per-scene loop
  else call failed
    alt timed out / caller abort
      GEN -> UI : throw (surface immediately, no fallback)
    else content moderation reject
      GEN --> UI : every scene refused (prompts kept,\nuser can adapt)
    else other error
      GEN -> UI : warn → fall through to per-scene loop
    end
  end
end

== 9. generateImage: pure-picture en-block ==
alt purePictures && pure descriptions derived
  GEN -> GEN : purePicturesPrompt(descriptions + consistency rules)\n— never the raw story prose
  GEN -> NET : ONE completion for all N pure descriptions
  alt all N images returned
    NET --> GEN : images ≥ count
    GEN --> UI : single scene with all images → done
  else fewer images returned
    GEN -> UI : warn → per-scene loop re-renders each description
  else call refused / moderated / failed
    GEN -> UI : warn → render each description per-scene\n(one reject can no longer cost the whole set)
  end
end

== 10. generateImage: per-scene loop ==
loop for each scene i while collected < total
  GEN -> GEN : scenePrompt(i) — planned description if any,\nelse storyboard instruction / anchor
  GEN -> NET : callOnce(renderMessages(prompt)) — prompt only,\nplus any reference-image parts; never the story history
  note over GEN, NET
    callOnce() network fallbacks, in order:
    1. modalities field rejected → retry WITHOUT it
    2. OpenRouter "No endpoints found … modality" → retry image-only
    3. model serves only /images endpoint → retry via /images
    4. context overflow → retry via /images (prompt only)
  end note
  alt call throws
    alt timed out / caller abort
      GEN -> GEN : mark ALL remaining scenes refused + stop
      GEN --> UI : partial result (anything collected kept)
    else refused / moderated / failed scene
      GEN -> GEN : record scene as refused (prompt + reason kept)
      GEN -> UI : continue with the NEXT scene (independent request)
    end
  else success
    GEN -> GEN : extract images
    alt no image parsed (unexpected shape / refusal)
      GEN -> GEN : record scene refused
    else images returned
      GEN -> GEN : collect; onProgress(done, total)
    end
  end
end
GEN --> UI : {content, images, scenes} — every scene has its\nEXACT prompt + refused flag; partials never discard images

== 11. Persist the result on the chapter node ==
UI -> UI : buildIllustrationAttachments(result, anchor)\n→ illustration-N.* + prompt-N.txt per image,\nrefused-prompt-N.txt per failed scene
alt zero attachments produced
  UI -> User : throw → alert "No image was created" + model reply
else
  UI -> SVC : editAssistant(chat, chapter, content, merged attachments)
  SVC --> UI : saved chapter → activate (scroll to it)
  alt imageCount == 0 (all refused)
    UI -> User : alert "No image was created" + reply
  else count > 1 && imageCount < count (partial storyboard)
    UI -> User : alert "Only got got/want of the scenes"
  end
end
UI -> UI : finally isLoading=false; pendingAction=null
note over UI
  Catch-all: any exception on the code path above
  → console.error + alert "Image generation failed".
end

== 12. Follow-up: adapt & re-render a refused prompt ==
note over UI
  A refused-prompt-N.txt stays attached, so the user can\nre-render one refused picture without re-running the dialog.
end note
User -> UI : "Adapt prompt & re-render" on a refused record
UI -> CFG : image-create model (or fallback image model)
UI -> GEN : generateImage(…, count:1, planDescriptions:false,\nscene = adapted prompt)
alt new image arrives
  UI -> SVC : replace refused record + old illustration\nfor that scene → editAssistant
else refused again
  UI -> User : alert with the model's reply (prompt kept for next try)
end

@enduml